<!--Post: 11142--><!--Time: 1110469972-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11142"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 7:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Begin speculation mode NOW over his computer knowledge or obvious lack of it. I mean there is no doubt the guy was named Dennis Rader or at least his posting name was, seems strange to make this name up over John Doe etc....It&#39;s archived so I can&#39;t get headers and the like past what is listed here... <BR> <BR>You could always try the email addy and see if anything pops back <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>From: <a href="mailto:dra...@ionet.net">dra...@ionet.net</a> &#40;Dennis Rader&#41; <BR>Subject: Windows98 freeze when connected to internet <BR>Date: 1998/09/03 <BR>Message-ID: &#60;<a href="mailto:35eeade3.304593@news.ionet.net">35eeade3.304593@news.ionet.net</a>&#62;#1/1 <BR>X-Deja-AN: 387707082 <BR>Sender: <a href="mailto:a...@tulnasb-08.ionet.net">a...@tulnasb-08.ionet.net</a> <BR>Organization: ioNET Inc. <BR>Reply-To: <a href="mailto:dra...@ionet.net">dra...@ionet.net</a> <BR>Newsgroups: alt.windows98 <BR> <BR>For some strange reason my new PC installed with windows98 freezes <BR>frequently when moving mouse and selecting features while on the <BR>internet. The keyboard &amp; mouse become completely inactive. My only <BR>recourse is to reboot the system. <BR> <BR>Any suggestions would be greatly appreciated. <BR> <BR>Thanks <BR>------------------------------------------------- <BR> <BR> <BR>Newsgroups: alt.invest.penny-stocks <BR> <BR>From: Dennis Rader &#60;<a href="mailto:dra...@ionet.net">dra...@ionet.net</a>&#62; - Find messages by this author <BR> <BR>Date: 1997/08/15 <BR> <BR>Subject: Test-JR <BR> <BR>Reply to Author  | Forward  | Print  | Individual Message  | Show original  | Report Abuse <BR> <BR> <BR>J.R.  <BR> <BR> <BR>I hope this method of seeking possible investment methods is useful.  <BR> <BR> <BR>D.R.  <BR>------------------------------------ <BR> <BR>  Mar 2 1997, 12:00 am     hide options <BR> <BR>Newsgroups: alt.unix.wizards <BR> <BR>From: <a href="mailto:dra...@ionet.net">dra...@ionet.net</a> &#40;Dennis Rader&#41; - Find messages by this author <BR> <BR>Date: 1997/03/02 <BR> <BR>Subject: Screen Saver <BR> <BR> <BR>Is there a way with xlock to view a screen saver like &#39;swarm&#39;?  <BR>----------------------------------------------- <BR> <BR>Dennis Rader <BR>  Mar 2 1997, 12:00 am     hide options <BR> <BR>Newsgroups: comp.unix.aix <BR> <BR>From: <a href="mailto:dra...@ionet.net">dra...@ionet.net</a> &#40;Dennis Rader&#41; - Find messages by this author <BR> <BR>Date: 1997/03/02 <BR> <BR>Subject: How can I activate swarm screen saver? THANKS :-&#41; <BR> <BR>Reply to Author  | Forward  | Print  | Individual Message  | Show original  | Report Abuse <BR> <BR>Please help me activate a screen saver in X windows called &#39;Swarm&#39;.  <BR>Thanks!  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11142-->
<!--Post: 11147--><!--Time: 1110477437-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11147"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 9:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am erring now towards this having been Denny himself. The reason is I checked up on ionet and it&#39;s addresses and phone show an Oklahoma location. Considering Wichita&#39;s close proximity to the Oklahoma border it&#39;s not a stretch for me to think these were posted after Denny got his first computer and internet account and was learning the ropes. I&#39;d originally rejected them as possibly being the one dude, but I&#39;m changing my mind.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11147-->
<!--Post: 11151--><!--Time: 1110479107-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11151"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 10:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I kinda sorta looking over them had the feeling they were his. Something in my long IT background told me Oklahoma or not, it was him.  <BR>  <BR>Did he actually progress from not being able to access his screen saver to posting on boards &#40;I sincerely have my doubts--certainly he was an avid newswatcher as well as detective book reader and they do quite a few stories now on cold cases and how computer &#39;DNA&#39; catches crooks he&#39;d know not to involve himself online. <BR> <BR>We now know he&#39;s not as smart as he thought he was &#40;his 6th grade level dog catcher case folder filled with horrid syntax, misspellings and other assorted mistakes---his lack of computer disk understanding&#41; so logging on and discussing his own case seems like a stretch to me---I could be wrong but I have a hunch he wasn&#39;t talking, he MAY have been READING and smirking...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11151-->
<!--Post: 11153--><!--Time: 1110479625-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11153"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lakesguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lakesguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 10:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, since he posted to alt.unix.wizards, maybe that&#39;s why Rader had to have his minister show him how to work the PC. Maybe BTK is a Unix guy! <BR> <BR>It&#39;d be interesting to see if this was him. I used to be a Unix sys. admin., and I know how anal other such creatures can be. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11153-->
<!--Post: 11202--><!--Time: 1110499046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11202"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 3:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There&#39;s a Dennis Rader living in Oklahoma City who is a completely different person than DTDC.  I think.  The Oklahoma DR is a Tai Chi instructor.  Maybe this DR is the Oklahoma City DR.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11202-->
<!--Post: 11203--><!--Time: 1110499240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11203"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 4:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->wow if i were him i would change me name<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11203-->
<!--Post: 11208--><!--Time: 1110503346-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11208"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 5:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m getting the feeling that the postings above from &#34;Dennis Rader&#34; are not &#34;BTK, Dennis Rader.&#34;  I say that b/c the writing seems too concise and fluid for  BTK.  There is a thread started under &#34;Media&#34; called &#34;BTK and Writing Analyzed&#34; which talks about his writing styles and possible dyslexia.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
